1
00:01:42,039 --> 00:01:49,009
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,950
[Episode 2]

3
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,310
Now I'll call roll in student ID order.

4
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:56,979
Let's all get to know each other,

5
00:01:56,979 --> 00:01:57,370
okay?

6
00:01:57,729 --> 00:01:58,979
-Okay.
-Okay!

7
00:01:59,370 --> 00:02:00,090
Lin Zhixia.

8
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:02,650
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

9
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:01,350
Here.

10
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:04,140
So you're Lin Zhixia.

11
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:04,470
Okay.

12
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:06,070
Jiang Yubai.

13
00:02:07,530 --> 00:02:08,940
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

14
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:10,259
Jiang Yubai?

15
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:11,710
Not here?

16
00:02:13,910 --> 00:02:14,770
Chen Zhenghao.

17
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:15,360
Here.

18
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:16,940
Wang Qingyu.

19
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:17,579
Here.

20
00:02:18,690 --> 00:02:19,290
Excuse me.

21
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:22,590
Late on the very first day?

22
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:23,620
What's your name?

23
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:24,810
Jiang Yubai.

24
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:38,960
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

25
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,600
Take the seat next to Lin Zhixia.

26
00:02:56,370 --> 00:02:59,990
[Reading Corner]

27
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:16,200
[Reading Corner]

28
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:53,170
It's been a long time.

29
00:03:54,090 --> 00:03:55,620
Yeah, it's been a long time.

30
00:03:59,780 --> 00:04:01,020
Hello.

31
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:07,210
My name is J-J-J-J-Jiang

32
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:08,580
Yubai.

33
00:04:10,410 --> 00:04:14,020
J-J-J-J-Jiang Yubai?

34
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:18,890
Then call me L-L-L-L-Lin Zhixia.

35
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:25,770
You've... gotten so tall.

36
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:29,190
Yeah, I-I grew up.

37
00:04:54,130 --> 00:04:54,730
Five yuan.

38
00:04:57,450 --> 00:04:57,930
Bro,

39
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,730
those are some pretty niche shoes.

40
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,420
You've got good taste.

41
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:04,600
Nah, I just threw them on.

42
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:07,920
I forgot to introduce myself.

43
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:08,930
I'm Duan Qiyan.

44
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:10,270
We're in the same class.

45
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:11,040
Aren't you Jiang Yubai—

46
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:13,170
the second-best student in our class?

47
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:16,830
Well, if you don't count Lin Zhixia,

48
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:18,400
you'd be first in our class.

49
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:22,430
How can we just leave Lin Zhixia out?

50
00:05:22,430 --> 00:05:23,690
She's the top student.

51
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,270
Still, it's different.

52
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:27,600
Her mind works on a whole different level.

53
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Not necessarily.

54
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,690
There's always someone better out there.

55
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,520
You're the first person I've met

56
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:38,530
who dares to challenge Lin Zhixia.

57
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,050
Just giving it a try.

58
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,310
I just noticed how tall you are.

59
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:44,640
Do you play basketball?

60
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:45,510
Yeah.

61
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:49,630
Me too.

62
00:05:50,070 --> 00:05:51,800
Let's play a game after school.

63
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:52,430
Sure.

64
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:53,659
Awesome.

65
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:57,360
Let's meet at the court after school.

66
00:06:19,930 --> 00:06:20,660
Jiang Yubai.

67
00:06:21,110 --> 00:06:24,240
I heard you transferred here
from a school in Singapore.

68
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:25,270
Yeah.

69
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,630
So, is school in Singapore

70
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:29,190
very different from ours?

71
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,600
Are there lots of foreigners there?

72
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:35,500
Actually, most of them are ethnic Chinese.

73
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,690
I heard littering is illegal in Singapore—

74
00:06:39,810 --> 00:06:40,540
is that true?

75
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:41,500
Really?

76
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,750
Maybe.

77
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,370
I've never broken the law,
so I'm not sure.

78
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:52,040
I read in a book

79
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:55,270
that Singapore is known
as the Garden City.

80
00:06:55,830 --> 00:06:57,390
Behind those strict regulations

81
00:06:57,390 --> 00:06:59,120
lies a kind of social contract.

82
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:01,040
Citizens give up a degree of freedom

83
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:01,560
in exchange

84
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:04,040
for an exceptionally clean
and orderly environment.

85
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,070
It's a city-state

86
00:07:05,070 --> 00:07:07,600
built through extraordinary planning

87
00:07:07,830 --> 00:07:09,270
under conditions of

88
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:11,070
extreme resource scarcity.

89
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:20,480
Why do you sound like
a robot answering questions?

90
00:07:52,830 --> 00:07:53,560
Jiang Yubai!

91
00:07:56,630 --> 00:07:57,680
Isn't it wild that we keep

92
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:58,830
running into each other?

93
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:00,690
Well, what are you doing tonight?

94
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,130
I...

95
00:08:03,130 --> 00:08:05,360
I was wondering
if you'd like to come over tonight.

96
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,070
We can watch

97
00:08:06,070 --> 00:08:07,800
the Lakers vs. Celtics replay together.

98
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,400
It's the game of the century.

99
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:22,580
What are you looking at?

100
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,360
Come on, let's go.

101
00:08:25,450 --> 00:08:26,770
I've got tons of snacks

102
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,500
and a huge sneaker collection.

103
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:30,230
We can check them out together.

104
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,169
Sure.

105
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:32,960
Let's go.

106
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:34,770
What do you like to do in your free time?

107
00:08:34,770 --> 00:08:36,460
Do you like playing soccer,

108
00:08:36,770 --> 00:08:37,510
video games,

109
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:38,730
or...

110
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:49,530
Jiang Yubai...

111
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:54,220
Why do I feel like
something's off with him?

112
00:09:01,390 --> 00:09:02,590
It's been a long time.

113
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:05,040
Yeah, it's been a long time.

114
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:08,670
Then what did you eat in Singapore?

115
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:11,390
Just food.

116
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:17,940
Why did I ask something like that?

117
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,700
Would he think I'm weird?

118
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,910
[Jiang Yubai]

119
00:10:34,770 --> 00:10:36,790
I got into
No. 1 High School's experimental class.

120
00:10:36,790 --> 00:10:38,790
We're going to be classmates again.

121
00:10:46,650 --> 00:10:47,460
Jiang Yubai,

122
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:49,230
I couldn't sleep,

123
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:51,400
so I got up to leave you a message.

124
00:10:52,410 --> 00:10:53,170
Honestly,

125
00:10:53,250 --> 00:10:54,340
I've imagined

126
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:56,030
our reunion countless times.

127
00:10:56,630 --> 00:10:58,370
But today's

128
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:01,500
was way more awkward than I expected.

129
00:11:02,170 --> 00:11:04,120
Maybe it was
because we couldn't keep in touch,

130
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:06,050
or maybe we'd been apart for so long

131
00:11:06,150 --> 00:11:08,750
that seeing each other again
felt unfamiliar.

132
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:11,580
Anyway, I want to be honest with you—

133
00:11:12,290 --> 00:11:14,600
things felt off between us today.

134
00:11:31,380 --> 00:11:33,370
Actually, I felt the same way.

135
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:41,130
[Lin Zhixia]

136
00:11:34,750 --> 00:11:37,480
I even bought strawberry milk
after class today,

137
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,660
but I've been too shy to give it to you.

138
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:47,950
[Jiang Yubai]

139
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:47,150
I can't let something
weigh on my mind overnight.

140
00:11:47,150 --> 00:11:48,550
It's so much easier
to just say it out loud.

141
00:11:48,010 --> 00:11:55,610
[Lin Zhixia]

142
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:52,100
Otherwise, overthinking is
just inefficient.

143
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:53,130
Haha.

144
00:11:53,890 --> 00:11:54,860
That's so you.

145
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,220
Why do you think

146
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:01,480
we have no trouble talking on QQ?

147
00:12:02,290 --> 00:12:03,090
That's weird.

148
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:08,530
Maybe we're just used to it.

149
00:12:12,050 --> 00:12:14,650
Anyway, I'll do my best to
get over it tomorrow.

150
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:16,410
Me too.

151
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,140
Let's ease into it.

152
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,580
There's one more thing I need to fix.

153
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:31,150
Today, when you asked
what I ate to get so tall,

154
00:12:31,650 --> 00:12:33,580
I just blurted out, "Food."

155
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,020
It was a pretty stupid answer.

156
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:37,900
I've been regretting it all day.

157
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:48,240
[Haha. Then answer me again.]

158
00:12:40,890 --> 00:12:42,270
Then answer me again.

159
00:12:54,750 --> 00:12:57,320
Actually, I was shorter than you
when we were kids.

160
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,050
That was a real blow to my pride.

161
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,000
So when I was abroad,

162
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,770
I made sure to
sleep by 8 or 9 every night.

163
00:13:01,770 --> 00:13:03,770
I worked really hard to grow taller.

164
00:13:06,940 --> 00:13:07,940
A little too hard.

165
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:09,900
You've overshot the mark.

166
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:27,520
What are you doing?

167
00:13:29,290 --> 00:13:30,580
I saw you were asleep,

168
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,410
so I didn't wake you up.

169
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:38,260
Who were you just chatting with?

170
00:13:39,150 --> 00:13:41,610
I had something urgent
to confirm, Brother.

171
00:13:42,390 --> 00:13:44,480
What was so urgent that
it had you grinning like that?

172
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,940
Let me see who you were chatting with.

173
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:47,150
It's the middle of the night.

174
00:13:47,150 --> 00:13:48,350
Who was it? Let me see.

175
00:13:48,390 --> 00:13:49,630
What are you doing?

176
00:13:49,630 --> 00:13:50,840
I want to see who you were chatting with.

177
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:52,790
-You can't invade my privacy.
-Let go.

178
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,080
Let go. Let me see.

179
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,320
The computer might break
if you just shut it down like that.

180
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,390
-It's fragile. It's...
-You...

181
00:14:01,390 --> 00:14:02,600
-It might break...
-You're the one who insists on looking.

182
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:05,330
-It could break like that.
-Keep your voice down.

183
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:07,340
I'm going to bed.

184
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,670
It's broken. It's broken.

185
00:14:08,670 --> 00:14:09,820
You can't just shut it down like that...

186
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:10,720
Lin Zhixia!

187
00:14:41,870 --> 00:14:43,870
J-J-J-J-Jiang Yubai.

188
00:14:54,390 --> 00:14:58,000
L-L-L-L-Lin Zhixia.

189
00:15:00,620 --> 00:15:01,150
Morning.

190
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:02,650
Morning.

191
00:15:07,370 --> 00:15:08,770
Ignoring air resistance

192
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:09,770
and friction,

193
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,170
suppose a car

194
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:13,460
is traveling at 30 meters per second.

195
00:15:14,050 --> 00:15:15,960
The driver notices a hazard ahead

196
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:18,840
and takes 0.5 seconds to react

197
00:15:19,010 --> 00:15:20,540
before hitting the brakes.

198
00:15:21,050 --> 00:15:23,320
If the hazard is 60 meters away

199
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:25,030
from the car's initial position,

200
00:15:25,030 --> 00:15:27,670
will an accident occur?

201
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,220
Tang Tingting.

202
00:15:31,150 --> 00:15:33,440
You answer. Will there be an accident?

203
00:15:39,050 --> 00:15:43,100
Will the car crash...

204
00:15:48,150 --> 00:15:48,650
Yes.

205
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,460
It will definitely crash.

206
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,060
Alright, you can sit down.

207
00:16:07,570 --> 00:16:08,480
You,

208
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:10,460
what's your name?

209
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:13,440
I'm Lin Zhixia.

210
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:15,700
Lin Zhixia,

211
00:16:16,150 --> 00:16:17,670
don't think I can't see you.

212
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:19,200
From the podium,

213
00:16:19,290 --> 00:16:21,220
I can see every little thing you do.

214
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,200
Were you even listening?

215
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,860
And yet you fed her the answer?

216
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:26,750
Go on, explain it.

217
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:28,880
Why will there be an accident?

218
00:16:31,150 --> 00:16:32,750
The car won't come to a stop

219
00:16:32,750 --> 00:16:34,030
until it's traveled 105 meters.

220
00:16:34,030 --> 00:16:35,630
Since 105 is greater than 60,

221
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:37,160
an accident is inevitable.

222
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,810
Ma'am, I was listening.

223
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:45,140
Alright, fine, you calculated fast.

224
00:16:45,770 --> 00:16:46,960
But you've been reading something
unrelated to class this whole time.

225
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,760
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

226
00:16:49,030 --> 00:16:50,960
What were you reading? Take it out.

227
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:03,010
You were reading this?

228
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:06,640
I've already studied 10th-grade physics,

229
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:09,920
so I wanted to read about things
I haven't learned yet.

230
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,180
Well...

231
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:14,790
even so, you still can't read it
during class, right?

232
00:17:14,790 --> 00:17:16,920
This still counts as outside reading.

233
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,619
That's all for today's class.

234
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:25,380
Class dismissed.

235
00:17:31,310 --> 00:17:32,770
If you're going to do
outside reading in class,

236
00:17:32,770 --> 00:17:33,570
you should...

237
00:17:34,830 --> 00:17:36,160
at least do it like this.

238
00:17:36,350 --> 00:17:39,880
You should be considerate of
the teacher's feelings, you know.

239
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:44,120
Does this really count as outside reading?

240
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,280
Let me see.

241
00:17:56,690 --> 00:18:00,090
[Introduction to Modern Physics]

242
00:18:18,590 --> 00:18:20,570
Yesterday, your Chinese teacher told me

243
00:18:19,610 --> 00:18:25,360
[Class Meeting]

244
00:18:20,850 --> 00:18:24,480
that you guys have been
a bit disengaged in class lately.

245
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:31,880
[Class Meeting]

246
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:31,330
I understand.

247
00:18:32,150 --> 00:18:34,420
Students in the experimental classes
have always

248
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:36,060
tended to focus more on
the science subjects.

249
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:38,090
[Class Meeting]

250
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:38,480
Your logical thinking skills
are quite strong.

251
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:39,850
So you're very used to

252
00:18:40,030 --> 00:18:41,350
the instant feedback that comes

253
00:18:41,350 --> 00:18:43,080
the moment you solve a problem.

254
00:18:43,810 --> 00:18:44,720
But students,

255
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,510
don't ever overlook

256
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:48,550
[Class Meeting]

257
00:18:46,510 --> 00:18:48,680
the gradual development of expression

258
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:51,540
and depth of thought
that studying Chinese brings.

259
00:18:53,110 --> 00:18:55,180
There's a tradition
in every class I teach.

260
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:59,130
[Class Meeting]

261
00:18:55,220 --> 00:18:56,810
At the start of each school year,

262
00:18:56,810 --> 00:18:59,440
I organize a Reading Corner activity.

263
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:00,830
You can each bring a book you'd recommend

264
00:19:00,830 --> 00:19:02,250
for the class reading corner,

265
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:04,510
and then we can all borrow and share them.

266
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:06,370
We can learn and grow together.

267
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,520
So you can start thinking now

268
00:19:08,550 --> 00:19:10,550
about the books you'd like to bring.

269
00:19:29,610 --> 00:19:31,410
Do you still like drinking this?

270
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:43,820
What are you doing? Let's go.

271
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:49,910
For the reading corner,
which book are you bringing?

272
00:19:50,850 --> 00:19:52,110
I haven't decided yet.

273
00:19:53,140 --> 00:19:54,570
I'm sure I'll recognize your pick

274
00:19:54,570 --> 00:19:55,630
the moment I see it.

275
00:19:56,250 --> 00:19:57,180
That confident?

276
00:19:57,880 --> 00:20:00,140
Then I'm sure I'll recognize yours, too.

277
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:04,380
You're still as competitive
as you were as a kid.

278
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:11,140
What?

279
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:15,290
How did you suddenly get so tall?

280
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:17,720
When we were little,
you were only this high.

281
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:18,640
Sorry,

282
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,650
but that's never happening again.

283
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:24,200
This is so great.

284
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:26,900
We're much more comfortable
around each other than we were yesterday.

285
00:20:26,900 --> 00:20:27,350
Yeah.

286
00:20:28,090 --> 00:20:30,070
Thanks to you—you always just say

287
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,610
what's on your mind.

288
00:20:32,030 --> 00:20:33,200
I held that in all day yesterday.

289
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,660
That was really unlike me.

290
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:37,400
You know,

291
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:38,860
I don't have many friends.

292
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:39,880
After you left,

293
00:20:40,270 --> 00:20:42,200
I tried making new ones.

294
00:20:43,590 --> 00:20:45,960
So I tried really hard to
start conversations

295
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:48,440
and ask people to go to
the bathroom together.

296
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:50,680
But after trying for a while, I realized

297
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:53,440
people just have their limits.

298
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:56,640
I'm just not very good at making friends.

299
00:20:57,740 --> 00:21:00,400
Like-minded people
naturally find each other,

300
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:02,080
so there's no need to force it.

301
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:04,680
See? Didn't we end up meeting again?

302
00:21:09,250 --> 00:21:10,590
I think you've changed.

303
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:11,850
How so?

304
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:18,480
I can't quite put it into words,

305
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:19,480
but you just have.

306
00:21:23,250 --> 00:21:24,910
What about me? Have I changed?

307
00:21:28,110 --> 00:21:29,510
Your hair is a bit longer.

308
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:31,500
Other than that...

309
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:32,940
not much.

310
00:21:37,030 --> 00:21:38,510
Actually, I've been wanting to ask you.

311
00:21:38,510 --> 00:21:40,240
Why did you come back this time?

312
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:41,360
Because of you.

313
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:46,160
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world came alive with color ♪

314
00:21:46,830 --> 00:21:51,200
♪ Could this be how love begins? ♪

315
00:21:51,290 --> 00:21:52,350
I mean...

316
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:54,700
♪ These unspoken feelings
are so hard to figure out ♪

317
00:21:53,750 --> 00:21:56,310
just like iron carbide, whose hardness

318
00:21:55,280 --> 00:22:00,680
♪ Hidden deep within your gaze ♪

319
00:21:56,310 --> 00:21:58,030
is 5 times that of ordinary iron,

320
00:21:58,030 --> 00:21:59,160
but ordinary iron

321
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:01,380
only turns into iron carbide
at high temperatures.

322
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:05,430
♪ Sometimes, I imagine
drifting beyond the skies with you ♪

323
00:22:01,830 --> 00:22:03,240
If I were ordinary iron,

324
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:05,980
you would be the high temperature.

325
00:22:05,980 --> 00:22:10,000
♪ Shimmering light
dances over the flower in bloom ♪

326
00:22:10,750 --> 00:22:12,240
I really came back because of you.

327
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:13,890
♪ After all we've been through,
our fates remain intertwined ♪

328
00:22:13,330 --> 00:22:16,250
Because I feel like I'm a better person

329
00:22:14,570 --> 00:22:21,060
♪ Perhaps fate favors me now ♪

330
00:22:17,250 --> 00:22:18,720
when I'm with you.

331
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:25,870
Where are you going?

332
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:28,560
This way, I'm taller than you.

333
00:22:33,070 --> 00:22:35,470
Now that you're back,
will you leave again?

334
00:22:39,430 --> 00:22:43,770
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world was filled with hope ♪

335
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,260
Definitely not while I'm in high school.

336
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:43,610
And

337
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:48,800
♪ Dim tender touches turn out to be love ♪

338
00:22:45,660 --> 00:22:47,320
we can go to college together.

339
00:22:48,350 --> 00:22:48,810
Okay.

340
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:52,150
♪ Unsettling thoughts at last unfold ♪

341
00:22:52,890 --> 00:22:58,170
♪ I return the moment you glance back ♪

342
00:22:58,610 --> 00:23:02,690
♪ If reunion is fated ♪

343
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:07,510
♪ Wish upon that dust speck
amid flowing light ♪

344
00:23:08,430 --> 00:23:11,500
♪ After all we've been through,
our fates remain intertwined ♪

345
00:23:12,180 --> 00:23:14,790
♪ If only time could stand still ♪

346
00:23:16,230 --> 00:23:17,890
My computer really is broken.

347
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:20,160
I'll tell Dad in a bit.

348
00:23:24,590 --> 00:23:27,120
My old back pain
is acting up again these days.

349
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:30,000
Once you finish eating,

350
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,310
take some food to your mom
at the supermarket.

351
00:23:32,310 --> 00:23:32,940
I'll go.

352
00:23:37,270 --> 00:23:37,830
Zhixia,

353
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:40,850
how's the start of the new school year?

354
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:49,520
Everything else is pretty good.

355
00:23:49,750 --> 00:23:51,200
But I don't know why.

356
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:54,540
Zeqiu won't let me say
we're siblings at school.

357
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:56,070
Lin Zhixia!

358
00:23:57,510 --> 00:23:58,090
You brat.

359
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:00,610
Is that how you act as a brother?

360
00:24:00,750 --> 00:24:03,000
You won't even let her
call you her brother?

361
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,460
She's playing the victim.

362
00:24:04,970 --> 00:24:05,750
Last night,

363
00:24:05,750 --> 00:24:07,270
she sneaked into my room
to use the internet

364
00:24:07,270 --> 00:24:08,530
and broke my computer.

365
00:24:09,090 --> 00:24:10,070
I didn't sneak in.

366
00:24:10,070 --> 00:24:11,870
I just didn't want to wake you up.

367
00:24:12,270 --> 00:24:14,720
Then who were you chatting
with in the middle of the night?

368
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:15,400
Who?

369
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:18,520
Who was it, Zhixia?

370
00:24:19,750 --> 00:24:20,550
Jiang Yubai.

371
00:24:21,550 --> 00:24:22,460
Jiang Yubai?

372
00:24:25,680 --> 00:24:27,940
Your deskmate from when you were little?

373
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:30,010
He's my deskmate again now.

374
00:24:30,350 --> 00:24:31,030
So what?

375
00:24:31,550 --> 00:24:32,950
Everyone has a deskmate.

376
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,440
Alright, stop arguing.

377
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:37,610
Finish eating quickly
and bring food to your mom.

378
00:24:42,570 --> 00:24:43,970
Dad, she won't let me eat.

379
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:45,090
I did not.

380
00:24:45,720 --> 00:24:46,550
You two...

381
00:24:56,590 --> 00:24:57,590
You're back, Mom.

382
00:24:58,270 --> 00:24:58,900
Yubai.

383
00:24:59,880 --> 00:25:01,400
You cooked for yourself?
What are you eating?

384
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:03,330
Just whipped up something simple.

385
00:25:04,010 --> 00:25:06,210
Are you getting used to the new company?

386
00:25:06,310 --> 00:25:07,110
It's just the beginning.

387
00:25:07,110 --> 00:25:09,970
I'm unfamiliar with the work,
but it'll get better.

388
00:25:10,270 --> 00:25:11,400
What about your colleagues?

389
00:25:11,400 --> 00:25:12,220
What are they like?

390
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:13,550
They are all quite nice.

391
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:14,890
That's good.

392
00:25:18,960 --> 00:25:21,290
I was supposed to ask you these yesterday.

393
00:25:21,510 --> 00:25:22,720
But look at you.

394
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:25,200
You ended up asking me everything first.

395
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:28,750
How about you?

396
00:25:29,270 --> 00:25:30,810
Are you getting used to the new school?

397
00:25:30,810 --> 00:25:32,470
Very well. I'm very used to it.

398
00:25:32,770 --> 00:25:34,570
It's way better than Singapore.

399
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:39,550
It seems you are very satisfied
with high school life.

400
00:25:44,640 --> 00:25:46,400
Your dad even said before

401
00:25:46,960 --> 00:25:48,550
that the divorce was between the adults,

402
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:51,280
so there was no need
to transfer you back to China.

403
00:25:51,790 --> 00:25:52,790
I told him

404
00:25:53,290 --> 00:25:55,240
that you definitely wanted to come back.

405
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:57,370
Your good friends are all here, right?

406
00:26:01,740 --> 00:26:02,440
Besides,

407
00:26:03,070 --> 00:26:04,870
you didn't like it there anyway.

408
00:26:06,270 --> 00:26:09,010
Right, my good friends are all here, too.

409
00:26:15,920 --> 00:26:17,480
What does "always arguing back" mean?

410
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:20,050
You say one thing,
and Tang Tingting fires back with nine.

411
00:26:20,050 --> 00:26:20,550
Your daughter is here.

412
00:26:20,550 --> 00:26:21,420
Mom, time to eat.

413
00:26:21,420 --> 00:26:22,220
Coming.

414
00:26:23,220 --> 00:26:24,140
You are so sweet.

415
00:26:24,140 --> 00:26:25,330
Bringing food to your mom?

416
00:26:25,330 --> 00:26:26,190
Hello, Auntie.

417
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:27,320
Good girl.

418
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:29,610
Right, I wanted to ask you, sweetie.

419
00:26:29,610 --> 00:26:30,470
Does your class

420
00:26:31,050 --> 00:26:33,510
assign seats based on grades?

421
00:26:34,940 --> 00:26:35,740
Well...

422
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:37,770
Since you two are
at opposite ends of the rankings,

423
00:26:37,770 --> 00:26:39,370
shouldn't you be deskmates?

424
00:26:40,900 --> 00:26:42,560
We aren't assigned like that.

425
00:26:44,090 --> 00:26:45,400
That's a real pity.

426
00:26:46,770 --> 00:26:47,970
That's okay, though.

427
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:50,420
Even though you've never
been in the same class,

428
00:26:50,420 --> 00:26:52,530
you grew up together.

429
00:26:52,700 --> 00:26:54,290
So you're best friends.

430
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,280
You need to keep an eye on her.

431
00:26:56,610 --> 00:26:58,250
She doesn't take studying seriously.

432
00:26:58,250 --> 00:26:59,380
You have to help her.

433
00:27:00,010 --> 00:27:00,680
Got it.

434
00:27:01,530 --> 00:27:02,380
I'm leaving, Mom.

435
00:27:02,380 --> 00:27:03,440
-Okay.
-Good girl.

436
00:27:04,810 --> 00:27:05,980
And one more thing,

437
00:27:07,070 --> 00:27:08,600
what is your favorite food?

438
00:27:13,010 --> 00:27:13,830
♪ Say hi ♪

439
00:27:14,140 --> 00:27:15,860
♪ We have different colors ♪

440
00:27:16,370 --> 00:27:18,110
♪ To me, say hi ♪

441
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:20,540
♪ We share the same dream ♪

442
00:27:20,870 --> 00:27:22,640
♪ How lucky I am to have you ♪

443
00:27:32,460 --> 00:27:33,140
Tingting.

444
00:27:37,590 --> 00:27:38,380
Sweetie.

445
00:27:39,460 --> 00:27:39,900
Mom.

446
00:27:40,980 --> 00:27:42,700
Look what I bought you.

447
00:27:42,790 --> 00:27:43,520
Take a break.

448
00:27:44,110 --> 00:27:44,740
You bought these?

449
00:27:44,740 --> 00:27:45,740
Have some snacks.

450
00:27:47,090 --> 00:27:48,460
Strawberry milk,

451
00:27:48,610 --> 00:27:50,740
strawberry cookies and strawberry candy—

452
00:27:50,740 --> 00:27:52,460
Which supermarket had a big sale?

453
00:27:52,460 --> 00:27:53,940
I-I don't like sweets.

454
00:27:53,940 --> 00:27:55,340
Sweets make me break out.

455
00:27:55,850 --> 00:27:57,770
I asked Lin Zhixia about this.

456
00:27:58,500 --> 00:28:00,230
Lin Zhixia told you to buy this?

457
00:28:01,530 --> 00:28:02,400
No.

458
00:28:02,740 --> 00:28:03,500
Here's the thing.

459
00:28:03,500 --> 00:28:05,440
I-I asked her very carefully.

460
00:28:05,830 --> 00:28:06,420
She told me

461
00:28:06,420 --> 00:28:08,750
she eats these almost every day.

462
00:28:09,530 --> 00:28:10,570
I was thinking,

463
00:28:11,050 --> 00:28:13,110
she's so smart,

464
00:28:13,330 --> 00:28:15,860
and it must have something
to do with her diet.

465
00:28:16,720 --> 00:28:18,310
Are you saying her smart brain

466
00:28:18,310 --> 00:28:20,250
comes from eating these?

467
00:28:21,530 --> 00:28:23,550
Well, what if it works?

468
00:28:24,140 --> 00:28:25,010
Let's give it a try.

469
00:28:25,010 --> 00:28:26,290
Just eat this one, okay?

470
00:28:26,290 --> 00:28:28,290
Mom, you're being ridiculous.

471
00:28:28,290 --> 00:28:30,620
Your ignorance could make the local news.

472
00:28:31,940 --> 00:28:33,440
Are you going to eat it or not?

473
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:34,810
I don't like sweets.

474
00:28:34,810 --> 00:28:35,810
I'm not eating it.

475
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:41,310
Your MP3,

476
00:28:41,810 --> 00:28:43,500
your phone,

477
00:28:43,500 --> 00:28:45,160
and all other electronics...

478
00:28:45,180 --> 00:28:47,180
I'll eat it. I'll eat it. I'll eat it.

479
00:28:47,330 --> 00:28:48,160
Well...

480
00:28:48,530 --> 00:28:49,940
That's more like it.

481
00:28:49,940 --> 00:28:51,610
It's food, not poison.

482
00:28:52,570 --> 00:28:55,430
Take a big bite.
Why are you eating it like medicine?

483
00:28:56,460 --> 00:28:57,720
Hurry, drink this.

484
00:28:57,770 --> 00:28:59,300
Wash it down with it. Hurry.

485
00:29:01,310 --> 00:29:02,480
Tastes good, right?

486
00:29:06,700 --> 00:29:07,300
Good girl.

487
00:29:08,380 --> 00:29:10,240
I'll buy you more when you finish.

488
00:29:11,090 --> 00:29:12,290
Eat it all. Eat it all.

489
00:29:18,790 --> 00:29:20,640
It tastes so bad.

490
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:23,510
I'll definitely break out tomorrow.

491
00:29:50,380 --> 00:29:51,330
About my book...

492
00:29:52,090 --> 00:29:53,090
Do you need a hint?

493
00:29:57,360 --> 00:29:58,680
[Natural Philosophy]

494
00:29:57,850 --> 00:29:58,380
This one.

495
00:30:02,700 --> 00:30:05,030
It's on the reading list
I gave you before.

496
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:15,680
[Jiang Yubai]

497
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:19,810
Have you decided what to read then?

498
00:30:24,050 --> 00:30:25,110
I've read them all.

499
00:30:27,180 --> 00:30:29,310
How many books have you actually read?

500
00:30:29,770 --> 00:30:31,500
I've read all the science ones.

501
00:30:35,530 --> 00:30:36,590
How about this one?

502
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:39,460
I've only heard of it but haven't read it.

503
00:30:40,420 --> 00:30:42,420
Jin Baihui has put that one in.

504
00:30:42,740 --> 00:30:43,800
Right, Jin Baihui?

505
00:30:47,810 --> 00:30:50,500
Jin Baihui, you read novels, too?

506
00:30:51,140 --> 00:30:51,980
I thought

507
00:30:51,980 --> 00:30:54,460
you'd put a study guide in here.

508
00:30:55,980 --> 00:30:57,940
It's the only non-academic book at home.

509
00:30:57,940 --> 00:30:59,670
I don't know when it was bought.

510
00:31:17,050 --> 00:31:18,530
[I blew the exam today. I got one
fill-in-the-blank math question wrong]

511
00:31:18,560 --> 00:31:20,170
[and only scored 118. But my parents
said not getting a perfect score]

512
00:31:19,980 --> 00:31:21,090
blew the exam today.

513
00:31:20,190 --> 00:31:22,010
[is the same as failing completely.
They even said I'm good for nothing.]

514
00:31:21,810 --> 00:31:23,420
I got one
fill-in-the-blank math question wrong

515
00:31:22,030 --> 00:31:25,090
[I've really tried my best.]

516
00:31:23,810 --> 00:31:25,180
and only scored 118.

517
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:38,850
[I'm so tired. I want to run away.
But where should I go?]

518
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,500
Whose book is this?

519
00:31:57,290 --> 00:31:58,150
Isn't it yours?

520
00:31:59,290 --> 00:31:59,740
No.

521
00:32:01,140 --> 00:32:02,270
That's impossible.

522
00:32:03,140 --> 00:32:05,330
You should be the only one
in the class who thinks

523
00:32:05,330 --> 00:32:06,590
a freshman in high school

524
00:32:06,590 --> 00:32:08,250
should read this kind of book.

525
00:32:26,700 --> 00:32:28,500
-This train of thought...
-Sir.

526
00:32:29,530 --> 00:32:30,180
Hold on,

527
00:32:30,180 --> 00:32:31,010
let me check.

528
00:32:31,460 --> 00:32:32,290
Let me check.

529
00:32:33,700 --> 00:32:35,290
You should consider

530
00:32:35,290 --> 00:32:38,250
taking university-level
math qualification exams.

531
00:32:38,250 --> 00:32:40,850
If you pass,
you can go straight to university.

532
00:32:42,180 --> 00:32:43,420
Actually, I haven't decided yet

533
00:32:43,420 --> 00:32:46,020
whether I need
to enter university this early.

534
00:32:48,330 --> 00:32:48,930
All right.

535
00:32:49,420 --> 00:32:51,680
Go back and discuss it with your parents.

536
00:32:52,420 --> 00:32:53,020
Off you go.

537
00:32:53,460 --> 00:32:55,640
All right, that's all from me.

538
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:06,050
Ms. Kong,

539
00:33:06,830 --> 00:33:09,090
can I take the math qualification exams?

540
00:33:09,680 --> 00:33:11,330
You just started
your first year of high school.

541
00:33:11,330 --> 00:33:12,660
Let's take it one step at a time.

542
00:33:12,660 --> 00:33:15,660
Isn't Lin Zhixia also
in her first year of high school?

543
00:33:16,180 --> 00:33:16,840
Here, look.

544
00:33:18,070 --> 00:33:20,140
Although you also
got a perfect score in math,

545
00:33:20,140 --> 00:33:22,530
Lin Zhixia solved the hardest
bonus problem

546
00:33:22,530 --> 00:33:25,130
and even came up
with two different solutions.

547
00:33:27,070 --> 00:33:27,700
In a while,

548
00:33:27,700 --> 00:33:29,900
there will be a provincial
youth math contest.

549
00:33:29,900 --> 00:33:30,920
If you get a good ranking

550
00:33:30,920 --> 00:33:32,110
in it,

551
00:33:32,220 --> 00:33:34,080
we'll talk about what comes next.

552
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:37,210
[Nanhai Province Star of Hope Math Contest

553
00:33:37,300 --> 00:33:41,040
[Contest Information]

554
00:33:54,740 --> 00:33:55,250
Oh no.

555
00:34:03,220 --> 00:34:04,290
Sorry, I'm late.

556
00:34:06,850 --> 00:34:09,840
The little genius finally
remembered her cleaning duty.

557
00:34:09,840 --> 00:34:11,300
Ms. Kong just called for me,

558
00:34:11,300 --> 00:34:12,480
so I was held up for a bit.

559
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:14,130
It's fine. We're almost done here.

560
00:34:14,130 --> 00:34:15,210
You guys go home.

561
00:34:15,210 --> 00:34:16,570
I'll take care of the rest.

562
00:34:16,570 --> 00:34:19,610
You immortals should stick
to solving the mysteries of the universe.

563
00:34:19,610 --> 00:34:21,650
Leave small things like cleaning

564
00:34:21,650 --> 00:34:23,650
to us mortals.

565
00:34:29,010 --> 00:34:29,870
Tang Tingting,

566
00:34:30,210 --> 00:34:31,210
every time you call me an immortal,

567
00:34:31,210 --> 00:34:32,690
it really makes me uncomfortable.

568
00:34:32,690 --> 00:34:34,489
Could you just call me by my name?

569
00:34:34,860 --> 00:34:36,500
You're already out of touch
with reality anyway.

570
00:34:36,500 --> 00:34:38,230
Isn't that what an immortal is?

571
00:34:38,380 --> 00:34:39,460
Is there anything else in your head

572
00:34:39,460 --> 00:34:40,880
besides studying?

573
00:34:41,190 --> 00:34:43,389
Stop meddling in us mortals' business.

574
00:34:45,500 --> 00:34:46,530
If you have any problem with me,

575
00:34:46,530 --> 00:34:47,590
you can just say it.

576
00:34:48,730 --> 00:34:49,530
Look,

577
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:51,570
I got these two big pimples on my face,

578
00:34:51,570 --> 00:34:52,730
all thanks to you.

579
00:34:53,190 --> 00:34:54,300
Can you stop telling my mom

580
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:55,440
all that nonsense?

581
00:34:56,050 --> 00:34:56,650
This is...

582
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:57,940
Zhixia,

583
00:34:59,340 --> 00:35:00,870
what is your favorite food?

584
00:35:03,170 --> 00:35:05,090
If strawberry cake
could improve intelligence,

585
00:35:05,090 --> 00:35:06,550
why not apply for a patent?

586
00:35:06,780 --> 00:35:08,090
Please tell my mom directly

587
00:35:08,090 --> 00:35:09,650
that your intelligence is genetic,

588
00:35:09,650 --> 00:35:10,940
and it can't be intervened.

589
00:35:10,940 --> 00:35:13,740
Tell her to stop making me
eat strawberry candies!

590
00:35:13,900 --> 00:35:14,830
That's not true.

591
00:35:14,860 --> 00:35:15,730
IQ heritability

592
00:35:15,730 --> 00:35:17,650
is around 40 to 60 percent.

593
00:35:17,860 --> 00:35:19,610
Genes have a strong influence,

594
00:35:19,610 --> 00:35:21,010
but it's not 100 percent.

595
00:35:23,130 --> 00:35:24,090
Oh my god.

596
00:35:24,090 --> 00:35:25,820
Now you're talking about this?

597
00:35:27,130 --> 00:35:29,060
Your mom asked me what I like to eat,

598
00:35:29,190 --> 00:35:32,010
but I didn't know she would buy it
and force you to eat it.

599
00:35:32,010 --> 00:35:33,210
The pimples on your face

600
00:35:33,210 --> 00:35:35,340
aren't necessarily from strawberry cake.

601
00:35:35,340 --> 00:35:37,380
It could be clogged pores caused

602
00:35:37,460 --> 00:35:40,460
by excess oil during puberty
and improper cleansing.

603
00:35:44,090 --> 00:35:45,650
Are you saying I don't wash my face?

604
00:35:45,650 --> 00:35:45,940
I...

605
00:35:45,980 --> 00:35:46,820
Wait.

606
00:35:47,500 --> 00:35:48,090
Tang,

607
00:35:48,610 --> 00:35:50,030
it's about time.

608
00:35:50,210 --> 00:35:50,860
We should go home.

609
00:35:50,860 --> 00:35:52,340
You don't need to smooth things over.

610
00:35:52,340 --> 00:35:54,940
Doesn't your dad
often compare you to her, too?

611
00:35:55,780 --> 00:35:57,400
It's fine. It doesn't bother me.

612
00:35:57,400 --> 00:35:59,460
Oh, so I'm the only one with a problem?

613
00:35:59,940 --> 00:36:01,010
Don't be like her.

614
00:36:01,010 --> 00:36:02,010
Stop pretending.

615
00:36:02,670 --> 00:36:04,230
Why are you yelling at me?

616
00:36:06,170 --> 00:36:06,980
Let's go.

617
00:36:07,460 --> 00:36:08,530
She already said

618
00:36:08,530 --> 00:36:09,790
she'd handle the rest.

619
00:36:09,860 --> 00:36:11,130
Might as well let her.

620
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:12,700
Let's go.

621
00:36:16,500 --> 00:36:17,700
Thank you, immortal.

622
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:19,060
Thank you, Lin Zhixia.

623
00:36:23,820 --> 00:36:24,460
Let's go.

624
00:36:32,670 --> 00:36:36,810
[Class Challenge Leaderboard]

625
00:36:33,690 --> 00:36:36,440
I can solve problems that others can't,

626
00:36:36,950 --> 00:36:40,540
[Gödel, Escher, Bach]

627
00:36:37,820 --> 00:36:39,020
but I can't figure out

628
00:36:40,150 --> 00:36:41,570
why I'm always

629
00:36:42,090 --> 00:36:43,350
an isolated solution,

630
00:36:44,790 --> 00:36:47,120
never part of anyone else's solution set.

631
00:37:04,300 --> 00:37:08,280
♪ With every breath, the shadows creep ♪

632
00:37:11,370 --> 00:37:14,570
♪ The devil in disguise ♪

633
00:37:15,970 --> 00:37:19,030
♪ Talking the sweetest lies ♪

634
00:37:22,940 --> 00:37:26,510
♪ It tries to drown me in my sleep ♪

635
00:37:29,160 --> 00:37:32,610
♪ And comes like a tide ♪

636
00:37:33,830 --> 00:37:38,430
♪ It hurts, but I'm too tired to hide ♪

637
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:43,940
♪ Please hold me, help me
walk out of this endless night ♪

638
00:37:42,340 --> 00:37:43,260
Growing taller

639
00:37:44,350 --> 00:37:45,630
♪ Lost the light and power ♪

640
00:37:44,380 --> 00:37:45,710
is of some use after all.

641
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:48,480
♪ Lost my will to fight ♪

642
00:37:47,530 --> 00:37:49,860
I find you always show up right on time.

643
00:37:48,890 --> 00:37:52,090
♪ Can you stay by my side ♪

644
00:37:50,500 --> 00:37:52,030
It's as if it was meant to be.

645
00:37:53,290 --> 00:37:56,170
♪ Be my light knight ♪

646
00:37:53,300 --> 00:37:53,860
What?

647
00:37:55,170 --> 00:37:57,490
I'm going to update
my Human Observation Diary.

648
00:37:57,490 --> 00:38:06,910
♪ Let's run away ♪

649
00:38:07,280 --> 00:38:09,890
♪ Towards the light ♪

650
00:38:11,030 --> 00:38:13,870
♪ With you, I'll win this fight ♪

651
00:38:15,210 --> 00:38:17,210
Let's make up for all the years
it stopped being updated.

652
00:38:15,790 --> 00:38:25,040
♪ Let's run away ♪

653
00:38:18,300 --> 00:38:18,920
How?

654
00:38:20,780 --> 00:38:23,110
Tell me what happened there.

655
00:38:23,380 --> 00:38:24,240
I'll record it.

656
00:38:25,910 --> 00:38:28,310
♪ No turn to black ♪

657
00:38:29,150 --> 00:38:33,120
♪ Your love will carry us
through the night ♪

658
00:38:34,390 --> 00:38:43,510
♪ Let's run away ♪

659
00:38:44,610 --> 00:38:45,960
♪ Towards the light ♪

660
00:38:46,010 --> 00:38:47,790
It turns out some understanding

661
00:38:47,790 --> 00:38:51,290
♪ With you, I'll win this fight ♪

662
00:38:48,690 --> 00:38:50,220
doesn't need to be rebuilt,

663
00:38:50,840 --> 00:38:52,230
even after years apart.

664
00:38:52,850 --> 00:39:01,970
♪ Let's run away ♪

665
00:38:53,820 --> 00:38:55,620
Just like after a system reboot,

666
00:38:56,900 --> 00:38:58,090
you are still my

667
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:00,570
default setting.

668
00:39:02,920 --> 00:39:05,220
♪ No turn to black ♪

669
00:39:06,110 --> 00:39:10,040
♪ Your love will carry us
through the night ♪

670
00:39:11,710 --> 00:39:15,640
♪ You and I ♪

671
00:39:16,310 --> 00:39:19,680
♪ Long last night ♪

672
00:39:21,060 --> 00:39:23,100
♪ You and I ♪
